<title>UK: New business is thin in Europe raw cotton markets.</title>
<headline>New business is thin in Europe raw cotton markets.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Currency factors again restricted the volume of new business in raw cotton in most European importing markets.</p>
<p>Attention was seen in selected African styles, particularly in Portugal and Italy, and Italy also saw transactions in Spanish new crop.</p>
<p>African cottons commanded most interest in Germany both for shipments nearby and through to next year.</p>
</text>
